it's been about four months since apple  revealed the iphone 13 lineup at their  september event and ever since i got my  hands on the 13 pro max i've been using  it every single day and i've gotta say  that i've never been as satisfied with  an iphone as i am right now with this  one so in this four month review i'm  gonna do something completely different  with the goal of helping you decide if  it's still worth upgrading to one of the  iphone 13 pro models or simply holding  off for the iphone 14 pro which has the  chance of coming with features like a  pill-shaped cutout instead of the notch  and maybe even a usb-c port like i  talked about in a previous video which  you should definitely check out but with  all that said the way i'm gonna do this  review is by making a list of every  single update or upgrade that came with  the 13 pro max and i'm gonna be sharing  my thoughts on which features actually  matter to me after 4 months of use with  the best features being saved for last  so let's get right into it first up we  have the changes that matter to me the  least like apple selling a one terabyte  iphone model which i definitely don't  need and things like the dual e sim  feature which don't matter to me since i  don't need more than one cellular line  there's also the new sierra blue color  which i really dislike so i ended up  going with graphite and i covered it up  with a leather skin from nomad which has  been incredibly impressive and resilient  and no they're not sponsoring this video  but getting back into the real new  features we have one that really didn't  matter to me at all and that's  photographic styles which allows you to  apply a pre-filter to all of your photos  but i honestly haven't touched this once  since my original review because i  personally like the default color  profile coming from the 13 pro so i  don't really need this feature after  that we have the new pro res recording  format and to me this is still a gimmick  because i don't really shoot videos with  my iphone with the intention of them  going into a professional video or  anything like that and since the file  size is absolutely massive i decided  that it's not even worth it for me to  enable that format for the everyday  stuff that i record like videos of my  kid now another upgrade we got this year  that apple didn't really talk about was  the fact that the iphone 13 pro max can  now accept up to 27 watts of charging  power so because of that i went ahead  and ordered an anchor 30 watt charger  just so i don't feel like i'm missing  out on potentially faster charging speed  but to be honest because of the  incredible battery life of this phone  which i'm gonna get to in just a couple  of minutes i haven't really been using  that adapter that much however when i  need to top up the battery quickly i'm  constantly blown away by how fast it  charges up compared to how long it used  to take a couple of years ago so this  new faster charging can definitely be  useful and now talking a little bit  about the cameras the selfie camera this  year got a small upgrade with some of  the features the rear camera gets like  prores recording but the one that i've  actually noticed is the jump up to smart  hdr4 which gives it a very noticeable  improvement in terms of high dynamic  range performance so now you're much  less likely to have blown out clouds in  the background which is a small but  helpful improvement and i also noticed  that sun flaring isn't nearly as bad of  a problem as it was last year so that's  very nice now one new feature that i  thought was going to be a massive game  changer is the new cinematic video  recording mode so i tested it out a few  times and i got some really cool looking  shots like this one of my wife and son  walking around downtown and i also  noticed that the stabilization is  absolutely incredible making it look  like you're holding a gimbal but  unfortunately it still has issues with  making it look natural since the blur  edging messes up sometimes and that  totally ruins the feel so in my opinion  this is going to be one of those  features that apple has to fine-tune  over the next few years but is just not  ready right now and because it's limited  to just 1080p quality i just can't get  myself to use it because i know that  this phone is capable of shooting in 4k  so i feel like i'm missing out in terms  of quality when i use cinematic video  mode next up we have the new macro mode  which was very impressive and exciting  when apple revealed it but i just  haven't been using it that much now  initially it was really messed up and  buggy because it worked automatically  and you couldn't control the lens that  it was switching to but apple quickly  fixed that issue and has added a button  for macro mode and it works like a charm  and what i really like about it is that  you can get some really cool shots like  this one of a toy car with a unique wide  angle perspective but still it's  sometimes hard to get the focus right if  you're too close but it can really help  you see details like the stamp on the  inside of this ring and for scenarios  like that this feature is awesome and  priceless now moving on to the next  feature the 13 pro now lets you manually  adjust the brightness up to a thousand  nits instead of last year's 800 which  has been very convenient for me in  situations where i want the display as  bright as possible since i don't like  using auto brightness and in terms of  the chipset this year's iphones also  come with the new a15 bionic chip with  the pro models getting the faster five  core gpu and while i haven't really  noticed a difference in snappiness  directly from the performance  improvement alone i've been testing out  some games and i've been really  impressed by the performance like for  example getting a solid 120 fps in games  like league of legends wild rift with no  hiccups at all and for other games that  are limited to 60 hertz i discovered  that you can enable low power mode and  still get perfect 60fps while saving an  impressive amount of battery life  compared to not having it on making it  the perfect mode for gaming and it's  only possible because of the high amount  of raw horsepower and efficiency with  the a15 channel and with that said let's  finally get into the main camera which  was upgraded with a better sensor and an  f 1.5 aperture lens to let in quite a  bit more light the level of noise  visible in photos is very very low  especially in dimmer situations and it's  just so much better than it was before  and in terms of daylight shots i've  never been so happy with photos coming  off of an iphone with them all being  super super sharp and in terms of  portrait mode using the main lens  everything looks absolutely amazing  especially with the really nice gradual  blur depth range as something gets  further away from the subject and i've  noticed that the camera can capture so  much color data like the natural sunset  hour glow with incredibly realistic  bokeh and even at night the night mode  portraits have been refined compared to  last year and they turn out amazing and  by far the biggest difference at night  is that the 13 pro match can perfectly  reproduce the natural glow and color  from neon lights which no other phone  can get right so yeah the camera  performance including the hardware and  the software has never been better and i  wouldn't choose any other phone's camera  over this one but an even bigger deal  that really matters to me is that this  year the ultrawide camera has been  upgraded with an f 1.8 aperture lens  compared to f 2.4 last year so it lets  in a ton more light and this led to a  massive difference in quality making it  actually usable now for lower light  situations and much more detail for  video recording as well so because of  all of this i'm using the ultra wide  lens much more often now compared to  last year with the 12 pro max so i'm  very happy about this ultrawide lens and  even better the new upgraded 3x optical  zoom lens is so much better than last  year's 2.5 x lens on the 12 pro max  which suffered from lots of issues with  noise so for the same reasons i hardly  ever used the telephoto lens last year  but now it looks very good and deals  with low light much better and on top of  that the new 77 millimeter focal length  is perfect for portrait photos making  them look closer to professional  portraits than ever before and i've got  to say that portrait mode with this lens  looks amazing with apple finally tuning  it perfectly while giving the background  a very natural blur including bokeh that  looks better than i've ever seen before  so overall i've never been more happy  with the camera performance and when it  comes to 4k video recording across any  of the lenses it's literally the best in  the business now moving on we have the  speaker quality upgrade with the  speakers having noticeably more volume  compared to last year which is very  important to me since i like to turn on  youtube videos while in the shower in  other situations and i no longer have  any issues with hearing what was said  but on the other hand the quality has  also received a huge improvement as well  with sharper highs and better dynamic  range between all of the frequencies and  this is really important to me since  there are so many use cases where i  simply use the built-in speakers instead  of reaching for my earpods and now  finishing off with the last three major  features that matter the most to me  after four months we have the much  improved heat management with the iphone  12 from max the display with dim and  various situations like just being on  the max a wireless charger just being  out in the sun while using apps just  turning the brightness all the way up to  the max and especially while gaming but  this year i've only witnessed the  display dim a couple of times during the  past four months compared to literally a  daily basis with the 12 pro max which  was extremely annoying and even if the  display does dim it usually only went  down to around 80 percent of the maximum  brightness compared to as low as 40  percent with the 12 which was insanely  dark so i'm very happy that apple was  able to fix this issue with the 13 pro  max and now for the second most  important feature we have the battery  life which has been absolutely  incredible and even mind-blowing at  times for the first time ever i no  longer have to even think about my  battery life because it's just so good  and it can literally last a day and a  half with regular use which never used  to happen before with any other iphone  and this matters to me so much because  it gives me a sense of freedom knowing  that i can play games at any time i want  without worrying about the battery life  at all in fact i completely stopped  charging my 13 pro max at night which  used to be something i had to do no  matter what with previous iphones to  make sure that it would last through the  next day nowadays it mostly just stays  topped up by using my car's mac safe  vent mount charger while driving and  using my convenient mac safe stand at  work with me only really having to  resort to wired cable charging on the  weekends and this level of battery life  is surprising coming from the 12 pro max  since that had decent battery life so i  couldn't imagine how it would feel  coming from an older or smaller iphone  to this one and now finally we have the  number one new feature that matters to  me the most and that is unsurprisingly  the 120hz pro motion refresh rate  feature which is exclusive to the pro  models for many years the chips have  gotten more and more powerful but you'd  never notice that big of a difference in  terms of snappiness because the refresh  rate of the iphone has always stuck to  60 hertz but now this 13 pro max feels  more snappy than any iphone i've ever  had solely because of once when he hurts  promotion especially for scrolling  through content like twitter and the  reason i know it matters to me so much  is because when someone asked me for  some help with their settings or some  kind of feature on their older 60hz  iphone the display looks so stuttery and  choppy that for a slight moment i think  that it might be broken or it might have  some kind of display issue before i  remember that it's actually a 60hz  display compared to 120 on the 13 pro  max and of course this has also been  very nice for things like gaming at  perfect 120fps and games like league of  legends making everything incredibly  smooth but my favorite thing of all is  apple's implementation of 120 hertz  using promotion which automatically  tunes the refresh rate down on the fly  to save battery life and while it's not  perfect all the time it's definitely  worth it and it's my absolute favorite  feature of the 13 pro max so there you  guys go hopefully you enjoyed my four  month review and if you did go ahead and  comment your thoughts down below and  definitely click the circle about to  subscribe for more videos like this one  and check out one of those two right  over there thanks for watching and i'll  see you in the next video  [Music]  you

